{"name":"Gloxinia","hex":"#693162","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gloxinia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Gesneriaceae – three species of tropical rhizomatous herbs, native to the Andes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gloxinia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gloxinia (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Gloxinia is a genus containing three species of tropical rhizomatous herbs in the flowering plant family Gesneriaceae. The species are primarily found in the Andes of South America, but Gloxinia perennis is also found in Central America and the West Indies, where it has probably escaped from cultivation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Gloxinia_perennis_08.JPG/330px-Gloxinia_perennis_08.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gloxinia_(genus)","wikidata":"Q5239844"},{"title":"Sinningia speciosa","blocks":[{"text":"Sinningia speciosa, sometimes known in the horticultural trade as gloxinia, is a tuberous member of the flowering plant native to Brazil within the family Gesneriaceae. Originally included in the genus Gloxinia in 1817, it was reclassified to Sinningia. Showy S. speciosa hybrids are still sometimes referred to simply as \"gloxinia\", although this name is now technically incorrect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Florada_da_Glox%C3%ADnia.jpg/330px-Florada_da_Glox%C3%ADnia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinningia_speciosa","wikidata":"Q163267"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Koellikeria_erinoides.jpg/500px-Koellikeria_erinoides.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Koellikeria_erinoides.jpg/500px-Koellikeria_erinoides.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoellikeria_erinoides.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mandirola_multiflora.jpg/500px-Mandirola_multiflora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mandirola_multiflora.jpg/500px-Mandirola_multiflora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowers of Mandirola multiflora","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMandirola_multiflora.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Dominance of Purple","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Dominance_of_Purple.jpg/500px-Dominance_of_Purple.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dominance_of_Purple.jpg","share":0.084375},{"title":"Purple lights, Party lights, Club wear, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Purple_lights%2C_Party_lights%2C_Club_wear%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Purple_lights%2C_Party_lights%2C_Club_wear%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5049019607843137,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Purple_lights,_Party_lights,_Club_wear,_Rostov-on-Don,_Russia.jpg","share":0.050625}]}}